Subject: [PATCH] gpu: allow ES2 fallback while collecting graphics capabilities

Chromium 156.0.8078.47 (1d17a2e2ee147bb7d6ae2ab6abdb3a2510c17775)
requests an ES3 context for GPU information and explicitly disables fallback.
On Mali-400, collection fails before filling GL strings or threaded texture
mailbox support. AwContents then forces auxiliary bitmap rendering, which
cannot display the normal HTML video layer.

Keep GLContextAttribs' default allow_es_version_fallback=true so capability
collection reports the real ES2 implementation. No ES3 capability is faked.

--- a/gpu/config/gpu_info_collector.cc
+++ b/gpu/config/gpu_info_collector.cc
@@ -91,7 +91,6 @@
 scoped_refptr<gl::GLContext> InitializeGLContext(gl::GLSurface* surface) {
   TRACE_EVENT("gpu,startup", "gpu_info_collector::InitializeGLContext");
   gl::GLContextAttribs attribs;
-  attribs.allow_es_version_fallback = false;
   scoped_refptr<gl::GLContext> context(
       gl::init::CreateGLContext(nullptr, surface, attribs));
   if (!context.get()) {
